{"_id":"68a7361b8ec3d8323af17315","nodeId":"_aA6Hp4KkgJeptqo8oKTg","roadmapSlug":"full-stack","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:06.907Z","description":"# Node.js\n\nNode.js is an open-source and cross-platform JavaScript runtime environment. It is a popular tool for almost any kind of project! Node.js runs the V8 JavaScript engine, Google Chrome's core, outside the browser. This allows Node.js to be very performant. A Node.js app runs in a single process, without creating a new thread for every request. Node.js provides a set of asynchronous I/O primitives in its standard library that prevent JavaScript code from blocking and generally, libraries in Node.js are written using non-blocking paradigms, making blocking behavior the exception rather than the norm.","resources":[{"type":"roadmap","title":"Visit Dedicated Node.js Roadmap","url":"https://roadmap.sh/nodejs","_id":"6a7f4a8ccb44947debcf7c39"},{"type":"official","title":"Node.js Website","url":"https://nodejs.org/en/about/","_id":"6a7f4a8ccb44947debcf7c3a"},{"type":"official","title":"Learn Node.js Official Website","url":"https://nodejs.org/en/learn/getting-started/introduction-to-nodejs","_id":"6a7f4a8ccb44947debcf7c3b"},{"type":"video","title":"Node.js and Express.js Full Course","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Oe421EPjeBE","_id":"6a7f4a8ccb44947debcf7c3c"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:04:12.015Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a2aca8ed5b55a91aab11124","title":"JavaScript Foundations","slug":"javascript-foundations","description":"The JavaScript you need before Node.js, frontend frameworks, APIs, and CLI apps.","lessonIds":["6a27367ad5b55a91aab0e0cc","6a273f65d5b55a91aab0e124","6a27f0dad5b55a91aab0e2a9","6a27ff2ed5b55a91aab0e378","6a280307d5b55a91aab0e3df","6a281cbfd5b55a91aab0e47b","6a2889f2d5b55a91aab0e7b2","6a294dfed5b55a91aab0e974","6a2965e0d5b55a91aab0f351","6a296e77d5b55a91aab0f382","6a2976e4d5b55a91aab0f66a","6a297985d5b55a91aab0f90c","6a297c52d5b55a91aab0fc67","6a29cb66d5b55a91aab10c0c","6a2ac002d5b55a91aa